  "findings": [
    "Clean steady loop: cameras off11.46ms; two cameras without peers13.67ms; real two-stream loopback15.59..15.70ms, p9521.31..21.63ms. These are controlled trials, not full UI/DDS runtime acceptance.",
    "Recurring measured state/CPU boundary:6 robot-state reads +4 payload-state reads +1 contact read per tick. Bridge plus payload takes4.74..4.93ms in detailed media trials; actual Pinocchio arithmetic is about.08ms per tick.",
    "One MPPI solve costs about8ms inclusive, including19 device_put calls totaling2.63..2.76ms and result wait/readback2.51..2.57ms. device_put is not19 equal PCIe transfers: two arguments already reside on device.",
    "Only6969host bytes enter these19 arguments. Frozen-input placement replay: serial2.171ms, tree1.703ms, packed0.344ms, including packed CPU concatenation and GPU completion. All values reconstruct exactly. This proves avoidable placement/API overhead; no live packed optimizer or end-to-end speedup has been validated.",
    "Native trace confirms many tiny copies/kernels. H2D/DtoH copy-engine activity sums to about.92ms over20ticks; API calls, allocation/indexing, dispatch and synchronization cost much more than moving these bytes. Trace overhead and other processes prevent interpreting activity sums as whole-GPU utilization.",
    "Clean physics host step is3.16..3.64ms with media; camera competition adds cost throughout the control and physics path, not only camera-submit time. A local receiver also contributes host load.",
    "The earlier.3s GC spike did not recur in the reduced-recording probes; active-loop GC stayed below.8ms. This does not establish behavior of long production sessions.",
    "Prioritize testing packed JAX inputs, then a shared/cached Genesis state snapshot and index buffers. Preserve contact, torque constraints and gait behavior; Pinocchio/model simplification is not the main measured target.",
    "The startup solve_hz=25 text is hardcoded; actual solve cadence is prediction_dt=.02 plus support-change solves. Call counts, not that log text, are used here."
